3.4:
May that day be darkness;
Let not God seek it from above,
Nor light shine on it.

3.5:
Let darkness and shadow of death redeem it;
Let a cloud dwell upon it;
Let the blackness of the day terrify it.

3.6:
As for that night, let thick darkness take it;
Let it not rejoice among the days of the year;
Let it not come into the number of the months.

3.9:
Let the stars of its twilight be darkened;
Let it hope for light but have none,
And let it not see the breaking dawn,

4.16:
It stood still, but I could not recognize its appearance;
A form was before my eyes;
There was silence, then I heard a voice:

6.4:
For the arrows of the Almighty are within me,
Their poison my spirit drinks;
The horrors of God are arranged against me.

7.11:
“Indeed I will not hold back my mouth;
I will speak in the distress of my spirit;
I will muse on the bitterness of my soul.

9.21:
I am blameless;
I do not know my soul;
I reject my life.

9.24:
The earth is given into the hand of the wicked;
He covers the faces of its judges.
If it is not He, then who is it?

10.1:
“My soul is loathed by my life;
I will abandon all restraint in myself to my complaint;
I will speak in the bitterness of my soul.

10.17:
You renew Your witnesses against me
And increase Your vexation toward me;
Hardship after hardship is with me.

11.20:
But the eyes of the wicked will come to an end,
And escape will perish from them;
And their hope is the expiring of their soul.”

12.3:
But I have a heart of wisdom as well as you;
I do not fall short of you.
And who does not know such things as these?

12.4:
I am a laughingstock to my friends,
The one who called on God and He answered him;
The righteous and blameless man is a laughingstock.

13.27:
You put my feet in the stocks
And kept watch over all my paths;
You set a limit for the soles of my feet,

14.5:
Since his days are determined,
The number of his months is with You;
And his limits You have set so that he cannot pass.

14.19:
Water wears away stones;
Its torrents wash away the dust of the earth;
So You make man’s hope perish.

15.30:
He will not be able to depart from darkness;
The flame will wither his shoots,
And by the breath of His mouth he will depart.

16.9:
His anger has torn me and hunted me down;
He has gnashed at me with His teeth;
My adversary sharpens his eyes to look at me.

16.10:
They have opened their mouth wide at me;
They have struck me on the cheek in reproach;
They have massed themselves against me.

16.12:
I was at ease, but He shattered me,
And He has grasped me by the neck and shaken me to pieces;
He has also set me up as His target.

16.13:
His arrows surround me.
Without mercy He splits my kidneys open;
He pours out my gall on the ground.

20.15:
He swallows up wealth,
But will vomit it up;
God will expel it from his belly.

20.25:
It is drawn forth and comes out of his back,
Even the glittering point from his gall;
Bouts of dread come upon him.

20.26:
Complete darkness is held in reserve for his treasures;
A fire unfanned will devour him;
It will consume the survivor in his tent.

21.33:
The clods of the valley will gently cover him;
Moreover, all men will draw up after him,
While countless ones go before him.

24.12:
From the city men groan,
And the souls of the wounded cry out;
Yet God does not pay attention to such offense.

24.13:
“Others have been with those who rebel against the light;
They do not want to recognize its ways
Nor abide in its paths.

24.14:
The murderer arises at dawn;
He kills the afflicted and the needy,
And at night he is as a thief.

24.16:
In the dark they dig into houses;
They shut themselves up by day;
They do not know the light.

24.18:
“They are insignificant on the surface of the water;
Their portion is cursed on the earth.
They do not turn toward the vineyards.

24.20:
A mother will forget him;
The worm feasts sweetly till he is no longer remembered.
And unrighteousness will be broken like a tree.

24.24:
They are exalted a little while, then they are gone;
Moreover, they are brought low and like everything gathered up;
Even like the heads of grain they are cut off.

26.14:
Behold, these are the fringes of His ways;
And how only with a whisper of a word do we hear of Him!
But His mighty thunder, who can understand?”

28.4:
He sinks a shaft far from habitation,
Forgotten by the foot;
They hang and swing to and fro far from men.

30.13:
They break up my path;
They profit from my destruction;
They have no helper.

30.15:
Terrors are turned against me;
They pursue my nobility as the wind,
And my hope for salvation has passed away like a cloud.

32.6:
So Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite answered and said,
“I am young in years and you are old;
Therefore I was shy and afraid to tell you my knowledge.

32.12:
I even carefully considered you;
And behold, there was no one who reproved Job,
Not one of you who answered his words.

32.13:
Lest you say,
‘We have found wisdom;
God will drive him away, not man.’

33.24:
Then let him be gracious to him, and say,
‘Deliver him from going down to the pit;
I have found atonement’;

34.31:
“For has anyone said to God,
‘I have borne chastisement;
I will not work destructively anymore;

34.32:
Instruct me what I do not behold;
If I have done injustice,
I will not do it again’?

34.33:
Shall He repay on your terms, because you have rejected it?
For you must choose, and not I;
Therefore say what you know.

34.37:
For he adds transgression to his sin;
He strikes his hands together among us,
And multiplies his words against God.’”

36.7:
He does not withdraw His eyes from the righteous;
But with kings on the throne
He has seated them forever, and they are exalted.

36.16:
Then indeed, He enticed you from the mouth of distress,
Instead of it, a broad place with no constraint;
And the comfort of your table full of fatness.

37.4:
After it, a voice roars;
He thunders with His majestic voice,
And He does not restrain the lightnings when His voice is heard.

37.23:
The Almighty—we cannot find Him;
He is exalted in power
And He will not afflict justice and abundant righteousness.
